# The build time variables the conf script reads, one per line. fab adds them
# to _CONF_VARS, which is how a unit contributes what a makefile fragment of
# the shared tree contributed with "CONF_VARS += NAME".
#
# PGSQL_PASS is the password the conf script gives the postgres role. A build
# that names none leaves the upstream default, 'postgres', which is why
# keel-postgresql removes the password afterwards: a layer is fetched by name
# and reused, so a known superuser password in it would be on every appliance
# built from it.
PGSQL_PASS
